148
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:51,857
Let's just hope that giant kissy-faced
lemon custard was telling the truth.

149
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:53,700
One way to find out! Yes!

150
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,160
It's them! Mimi?

151
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:03,020
Tentomon and Izzy! Hey!

152
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,450
Hi, Mimi.

153
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:07,360
Finally, a friendly face!

154
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,317
Where's the rest of the gang?

155
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,420
I've no idea.

156
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:14,237
But, uh, shouldn't we, like,
look for them or something?

157
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,908
What are you doing, anyway?

158
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:19,299
Right now, I'm trying to
decipher these hieroglyphs.

159
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,757
Well, can't that wait, if
you don't mind my asking?

160
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:23,097
That's what I keep telling him.

161
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:25,917
Let's go and look for the others,
I say, but does he listen to me?

162
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:26,830
No.

163
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,492
All right, get up, Izzy.

164
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:31,677
I'm sure the key to figuring
everything out is in here.

165
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:36,140
The question is, does each glyph
represent a letter, a word, or a phrase?

166
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:39,962
I'll have to cross-reference
the characteristics.

167
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,937
Izzy, any idea how long
this is going to take?

168
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:50,920
I mean, can we go sometime
before winter sets in?

169
00:08:51,540 --> 00:08:52,370
Izzy?

170
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:55,289
Izzy, your friend is
asking you a question.

171
00:08:56,040 --> 00:09:00,117
Yeah, her rear end's getting cold,
sitting on the stone floor, doing nothing.

172
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,520
Oh, wait, wait.

173
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:03,547
Yeah, yeah, that might work.

174
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:06,160
Uh-oh, Izzy?

175
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:09,900
Are you ignoring me, you
computer geek pipsqueak?

176
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:14,457
Okay, so if I make the variable constant
and search for bottle patterns...

177
00:09:14,540 --> 00:09:16,140
Hey, here's something.

178
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:19,950
Prodigious!

179
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:21,664
These ruins are a gigantic maze

180
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:24,040
I'm leaving!

181
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:25,560
Right now!

182
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:34,417
Don't try, Mimi Oh no, not you
too Izzy, do something Do what?

183
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:39,265
My laptop can't do everything I don't
know, tell her you're sorry Sorry for what?

184
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,957
I can't take it anymore I haven't had

185
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,997
anything to eat in my
feet You're killing me in

186
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,577
a giant limit because
you're trying to kiss

187
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:47,417
me and all I want to
do is get out of here.

188
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:48,330
You just want to leave.

189
00:09:48,413 --> 00:09:49,300
Is that so wrong?

190
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:53,066
Honestly, Izzy, how can
you be so insensitive?

191
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,150
Insensitive?

192
00:09:54,233 --> 00:09:55,063
What do you mean?

193
00:09:55,146 --> 00:09:57,497
You ignore us while you
poke away at your computer.

194
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:58,677
I'm not ignoring you.

195
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:01,917
I'm doing something ultra-important,
like maybe saving this world.

196
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,857
If I can just decipher these
hieroglyphs, then maybe we could...

197
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:07,116
You escape your stupid hieroglyphics.

198
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:08,180
Mimi, wait.

199
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:11,117
You just like playing on
your computer, that's all.

200
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,777
You think I'm just playing around here?

201
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:15,860
I almost think you like
computers more than people.

202
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:20,945
Don't look now, but Mimi
and Tentomon are gone.

203
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:22,119
Now what do we do?

204
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,640
I hate this place.

205
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:27,177
I'll never recommend
this resort to anyone.

206
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:28,120
Mimi, wait.

207
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,320
Oh, dear. Mimi.

208
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:33,857
Mimi, are you all right?

209
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:35,340
I'm not a bad person.

210
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:38,179
So why is all this happening to me?

211
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:40,185
Mimi, we've got to be careful.

212
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:42,777
One wrong turn and we
can get lost in here.

213
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:46,517
All I want to do is get back
home. That's all. Please, wait.

214
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,757
I really think we ought
to find our way back.

215
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:51,160
I want my own bed, my own bathroom.

216
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:53,337
I'm even starting to miss my baby brother.

217
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:54,817
Please, stop running off.

218
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,397
I don't see them anywhere.

219
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:58,068
Where could they have gone?

220
00:10:58,980 --> 00:11:01,397
They didn't go deeper
into the maze, did they?

221
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,598
That'd be my guess.

222
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:06,817
These deciphered hieroglyphs tell me the
inside of these ruins is a giant labyrinth.

223
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:10,540
So if that is the case, they
could be lost in there forever.

224
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,300
Forever? Oh.

225
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:35,020
Hey, uh, Tentabon? Yes?

226
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:37,997
You get the feeling we're sort
of going around in circles?

227
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:38,910
Hmm.

228
00:11:38,993 --> 00:11:40,517
See this sooty smudge on the wall?

229
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,577
I remember passing it a long time ago.

230
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:43,490
You're right.

231
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:45,197
Could it be that we're lost?

232
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:50,420
I realize this is probably a bad time
to say I told you so, but... Oh, quiet!

233
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,517
Oh, I can't bear it.

234
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:54,430
I'm going in.

235
00:11:54,513 --> 00:11:56,240
And get lost, too? No, Palmon.

236
00:11:56,380 --> 00:11:58,117
We have got to use our heads first.

237
00:11:58,200 --> 00:12:00,800
But we can't just leave them. We won't.

238
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:03,254
But this is one super complicated maze.

239
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,675
I've got to try to get a handle on it.

240
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,059
Then maybe I can help get them out.

241
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,900
Well, being lost isn't so bad.

242
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:13,780
Great. Oh, dear. Are you hurt?

243
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:15,800
No, I'm fine.

244
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,657
I'm getting used to it by now.

245
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:20,477
If I'd just got to chill it and kept,
none of this would have happened.

246
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:22,817
Let's try a systematic approach to this.

247
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:26,417
Maybe if we just keep turning to
the left or something like that...

248
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:27,717
Why should I listen to you?

249
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:30,677
It's your friend Izzy that got me
into this mess in the first place.

250
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:32,317
Wait, don't be too hard on him.

251
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:33,230
Yes,

252
00:12:33,313 --> 00:12:34,143
he gets a little wrapped
up in his work and

253
00:12:34,226 --> 00:12:35,957
doesn't always interact well with others,

254
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:37,280
but he's a good boy.

255
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:39,460
There they are.

256
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:44,221
That's Mimi, that blinking light?

257
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:45,450
Precisely.

258
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,420
No, no, not that way.

259
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,680
I'll buzz off. Leave me alone.

260
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:51,460
That's my girl.

261
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:54,297
I've honed in on the
signal from her digivice.

262
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,440
We can hear her.

263
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,268
Let's hope she can hear us.

264
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:00,446
Izzy to Mimi, do you read me?

265
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:02,077
Repeat, do you read me?

266
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,220
Izzy, is that you?

267
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,932
Oh, right, it's working.

268
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:09,717
Okay, Mimi, I'm going to navigate for
you, so walk exactly where I tell you to.

269
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:11,237
Don't worry, it'll be okay.

270
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:13,077
Hey, he knows what he's doing.

271
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,395
Is that you, pal mom?

272
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:17,657
Just do what Izzy tells you and you'll
be out of there before you know it.

273
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:19,660
I told you Izzy was a good boy.

274
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,837
Okay, now take the first
doorway on the right.

275
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,737
When you get to the end, turn left.

276
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:26,197
But be careful of the next room because

277
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:28,986
there's a big hole in
the middle of the floor.

278
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,393
There should be a narrow ledge
you can use to get across.

279
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,589
Izzy, did we have to
take the scenic route?

280
00:13:45,820 --> 00:13:46,650
Uh-oh.

281
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:48,312
What do you mean, uh-oh?

282
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:49,820
Kate, I'm ready.

283
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,313
Which way should we go?

284
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,013
Something has happened.

285
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,780
I was hoping it was just a glitch.

286
00:13:56,620 --> 00:14:00,497
But there's definitely something in that
maze with them, and it's moving closer.

287
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,180
Now I am starting to worry.

288
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,794
Izzy, what's with the silent treatment?

289
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:06,660
Did you hear that?

290
00:14:06,840 --> 00:14:08,340
It sounded evil.

291
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:11,237
Gentlemen, it's been such a long time.

292
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,540
Oh, no!

293
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:17,110
St.

294
00:14:17,193 --> 00:14:19,360
Deramon, half man, half horse.

295
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:22,920
You really don't want to get
on either of his bad sides.

296
00:14:25,860 --> 00:14:26,800
Mimi, run!

297
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:28,180
I like a good chase.

298
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:29,360
Take a lap!

299
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:37,220
Izzy, we are quite anxiously awaiting
your directions. Are you there?

300
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,617
Another lap, through the doorway.

301
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:40,582
This way, Mimi.

302
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,400
Great job, Izzy.

303
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:44,370
It's the dead end.

304
00:14:44,453 --> 00:14:45,691
Where do we go now, Izzy?

305
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:47,320
Izzy, hello.

306
00:14:48,400 --> 00:14:50,277
We seem to have lost contact with him.

307
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,040
Oh, really? He's back.

308
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:53,800
Solar rain.

309
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:56,050
Fire.

310
00:14:58,740 --> 00:15:00,140
Look at my skirt.

311
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:01,457
Look at that now.

312
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:02,658
Get out of the way.

313
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:08,742
Your bravery is noted, but that
alone will not gain you any mercy.

314
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:10,137
What are you waiting for?

315
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,237
Make yourself bigger.

316
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:14,597
If you mean you want me to digivolve,
I'm afraid that's impossible.

317
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:16,197
What do you mean, impossible?

318
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:17,657
I'll tell you what he means.

319
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:22,377
He cannot protect you, so you have to hold
your ground, and that's truly impossible.

320
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:23,290
Stop talking!

321
00:15:23,373 --> 00:15:24,203
Get throwing!

322
00:15:24,286 --> 00:15:27,117
Oh, how I'd like to, but if I'm
separated from Izzy, I can't.

323
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:28,460
Ah! Stop that!

324
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:31,659
Can't you see I'm in the
middle of saying something?

325
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:32,995
What's that practice?

326
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:38,650
Izzy!

327
00:15:38,733 --> 00:15:39,697
Get out of there!

328
00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:40,617
Hurry! Come on!

329
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:42,582
You don't have to tell me twice!

330
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:43,840
Watch out, Eevee!

331
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:05,680
Helmon Digivolve to!

332
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,030
Tokomon!

333
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,860
Leave my friends alone!

334
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:18,620
Mimi, get back!

335
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,900
Leave this to me!

336
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,220
Testamon, Digivolve, too!

337
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:28,330
Kabuterimon!

338
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:32,860
Oh, I forgot.

339
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,237
When you get bigger, you
get a lot bigger, don't you?

340
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,740
Watch where you step!

341
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,060
Oh, uh, sorry.

342
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:49,377
That's one way to get out of there.

343
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:52,277
Yeah, but this is no time for
us to start taking it easy.

344
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:53,460
Look who's here.

345
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,420
Yeah, I see him.

346
00:16:55,540 --> 00:16:56,700
Leave them alone!

347
00:16:58,920 --> 00:16:59,802
ElectroShocker!

348
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:02,400
I think it's time for a needle spray!

349
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,120
That felt interesting.

350
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:17,147
One of those black ears
fell out of his body.

351
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:22,360
Where am I?

352
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:26,080
Are you a good Digimon now? What?

353
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,000
That device on your bag.

354
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:30,750
This?

355
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:32,300
I have seen it before.

356
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:36,680
It is the mystical symbol of the Digivice.

357
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:40,000
These ruins are its temple,
and I am its guardian.

358
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:43,518
Well, that certainly looks familiar.

359
00:17:43,620 --> 00:17:45,937
The Digivice is a preserver of the light,

360
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:50,079
a last line of defense against the
darkness that threatens existence.

361
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:51,250
Really?

362
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,640
I didn't get that,

363
00:17:52,760 --> 00:17:56,642
but I'm starting to think they're
more than just a cool accessory.

364
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:58,900
Leomon, why are you here?

365
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:04,320
To destroy them, the children. What?

366
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:08,180
I warn you, Centarumon,
do not interfere with me.

367
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:13,240
No, Leomon!

368
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:18,360
I can't look, it's too
scary! Well, maybe a peek.

369
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,800
Whoa, time's standing still here.

370
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:23,940
I said no, Leomon!

371
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:26,337
The children possess the Digivice!

372
00:18:26,420 --> 00:18:29,980
As the guardian of its temple,
I must protect them as well.

373
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,820
Protect them from me?

374
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:33,960
Good luck.

375
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:36,600
Fist of the Beast King!

376
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:38,280
Solar Ray!

377
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:44,460
Now let's stop this madness
before one of us is hurt.

378
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:45,850
Viamond?

379
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,960
The children must be destroyed

380
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:02,910
No!

381
00:19:02,993 --> 00:19:04,621
You must meet some other children

382
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:09,520
Your digivice can stop him in his tracks

383
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:13,200
Bad kitty! Ow! Go on! Ow!

384
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:29,209
Well, that got rid of him.

385
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:31,773
These things really are kind of amazing.

386
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:35,180
A preserver of light against the darkness.

387
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:36,777
Can you order a pizza with it?

388
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:37,978
I'm still starving.

389
00:19:40,620 --> 00:19:43,917
Centarumon, maybe with your help,
we could stop this black ear.

390
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:44,830
No,

391
00:19:44,913 --> 00:19:47,037
I'm afraid I have neither
the strength nor the

392
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:50,355
knowledge to oppose Devimon
and the powers of darkness.

393
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:52,517
Are you still going on about that?

394
00:19:52,600 --> 00:19:54,817
When can we start looking
for something to eat?

395
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:56,597
Guess I'll just have to keep deciphering

396
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:59,268
and analyzing these two
sets of hieroglyphs.

397
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:02,125
I'm sure all the answers
are in here somewhere.

398
00:20:02,540 --> 00:20:04,377
Excuse me, isn't this where I came in?

399
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:06,417
You're not seriously
starting all that again?

400
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:08,480
Not right now. Just a nano.

401
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:10,460
This black gear?

402
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:12,257
Who cares about that dumb old thing?

403
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:13,516
All I want is lunch!

404
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:25,180
Look, the process has reversed itself.

405
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:26,550
Amazing!

406
00:20:26,820 --> 00:20:28,055
Excellent work, Mimi.

407
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:32,017
It just goes to show you that sometimes
the simplest solution is actually the best.

408
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,717
That's not much of a compliment.

409
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:36,320
Oh yeah, I knew you couldn't keep away.

410
00:20:38,660 --> 00:20:40,836
So are we gonna go on a date or what?

411
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:42,617
Come on, what's your phone number?

412
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,440
Man, he is persistent!

413
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,880
At least blow us a kiss! Okay!

414
00:20:49,060 --> 00:20:50,300
Oh, come on!

415
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:51,797
Do it like you mean it!

416
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,586
You know you like us,
you know you do, please!

417
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:28,040
I wish, do you think you're here?

418
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:30,157
I wish, do you think you're here?

419
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:31,817
Tell me, do you think you're here?

420
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:34,337
Right now, you can't see anything.

421
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:36,760
It's not all that it's all

422
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:44,600
It's cold, so it's cold
It's a jacket with my hands

423
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:56,317
forget The sun will

424
00:21:56,400 --> 00:22:01,600
shine I'll never forget

425
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:07,220
It's so warm, that day, that time

426
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:13,377
I want a wish for a wish
for a wind When I put the

427
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:15,537
wind in the wind I can't

428
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:21,700
see the tomorrow's future,

429
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:25,357
I'm sure...

430
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:32,357
I wish you I wish I

431
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:39,060
could.

432
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:02,390
Let's go.
